<title>USA: Israel Electric raises $600 mln of debt securities.</title>
<headline>Israel Electric raises $600 mln of debt securities.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Israel Electric Corp said Thursday that it raised $600 million from its its debt securities offering for 10, 30 and 100 years in U.S. markets.</p>
<p>The sum exceeded the government-owned company's expectations of raising $400 million in bond issues.</p>
<p>The company, the first Israeli government company to sell bonds in the United States and Europe, said it was the first time it issued 100- and 30-year debt securities.</p>
</text>
